==================================================================================
TOURNAMENTS AS INTRANSITIVITY AMONG n THINGS (mac-mini-S34)
==================================================================================

[1] A preference among n things splits: ORDER (rankable part) (+) INTRANSITIVITY (the rest):
     n pairs C(n,2)  ORDER dim (n-1)  INTRANSIT dim C(n-1,2)
     3            3                2                       1
     4            6                3                       3
     5           10                4                       6
     6           15                5                      10
     7           21                6                      15
    ORDER = cut space (a ranking potential, a COBOUNDARY); INTRANSITIVITY = cycle space (H^1).
    => the n-1 'score' d.o.f. are the orderable part; the C(n-1,2) cycle d.o.f. are pure
       intransitivity -- the part NO ranking can explain. Intransitivity DOMINATES for large n.

[2] INTRANSITIVITY SPECTRUM -- cyclicity (# rock-paper-scissors triples) per iso class:
    n=3: cyclicity -> #classes {0: 1, 1: 1}; TRANSITIVE (c=0): 1 class (unique, the cusp); max intransitivity c=1
    n=4: cyclicity -> #classes {0: 1, 1: 2, 2: 1}; TRANSITIVE (c=0): 1 class (unique, the cusp); max intransitivity c=2
    n=5: cyclicity -> #classes {0: 1, 1: 3, 2: 2, 3: 2, 4: 3, 5: 1}; TRANSITIVE (c=0): 1 class (unique, the cusp); max intransitivity c=5
    n=6: cyclicity -> #classes {0: 1, 1: 4, 2: 4, 3: 4, 4: 10, 5: 8, 6: 12, 7: 8, 8: 5}; TRANSITIVE (c=0): 1 class (unique, the cusp); max intransitivity c=8
    => c=0 (transitive = the ONE total order up to relabeling) is unique; everything else is
       intransitive. The metagraph is organized by intransitivity: 0 at the center (cusp).

[3] ORDERABILITY vanishes (intransitivity is GENERIC) -- the Condorcet phenomenon:
     n  P(transitive=fully orderable)   P(has a Condorcet winner)
     3                       0.750000                    0.750000
     4                       0.375000                    0.500000
     5                       0.117188                    0.312500
     6                       0.021973                    0.187500
     7                       0.002403                    0.109375
     8                       0.000150                    0.062500
    => both -> 0 fast: a random preference among many things is almost never rankable and
       usually has no overall winner. INTRANSITIVITY is the rule, not the exception.

[4] # of DISTINCT intransitivity patterns (GF(2) cycle-space shadow, up to relabeling):
    The undirected support of the intransitivity = an EVEN graph (cycle space). Iso classes:
    A002854 = 2, 3, 7, 16, 54 (n=3..7) = the # of essentially different intransitivity SHAPES.
    (Tournaments A000568 = 2,4,12,56,456 > these: a shape hosts several preferences once you
    overlay an ordering -- order x intransitivity, the labeled 2^(n-1) fibration, S32/HYP-3595.)

==================================================================================
THE ATOM: the 3-cycle (odd, length 3) = the irreducible intransitivity = the Condorcet paradox.
Tournaments ARE the space of intransitivity patterns among n things; the transitive order is the
trivial (cohomologically exact) point; the odd cycle generates H^1. The LRC danger relation among
RUNNERS is the same kind of object -- intransitivity among n things -- and its apex odd cycle C_7
is the irreducible resonance the floor 4cos^2(3pi/7)>0 (THM-590) certifies as non-degenerate.
==================================================================================
